          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@%2$@ dB"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, %@" : {
      "comment" : "A braille table in words: its code's name, then how it contracts, in lower case. %1$@ is the code's name, such as Unified English Braille, and %2$@ the contraction, such as uncontracted (Grade 1).\nA heading's description followed by a detail such as its duration. %1$@ is the description, such as \"Chapter One - level 1\"; %2$@ is the detail, such as \"4 minutes\".\nA language's menu item in the transcription language pop-up, with its speech model's status. %1$@ is the language's name, such as \"English (United States)\"; %2$@ is the status: installed, needs download, or not supported.\nJoins a name and a note about it with a comma, such as an encoding or braille code and \"guessed\". %1$@ is the name and %2$@ the note.\nJoins two parts of a label with a comma. %1$@ is the text so far and %2$@ the next part. English puts a comma and a space between them.\nText of the Library window's View pop-up and Go to View. What a window says on going to the view name by Go to View's key or menu item: the name, then counts, what the view lists there (CountWording.listItems(of:feeds:)), as \"All Items, 743 books, 2 feeds\". Placeholders in order: name, counts.\nThe microphone level spoken in the Record window. %1$@ is the level in decibels in words, such as \"minus 12 decibels\", and %2$@ is a word for how loud that is, such as \"good\".\nThe right side of a row in the Library views settings: whether the view is built in or custom, then when it shows. %1$@ is built in or custom and %2$@ is its visibility, such as \"always\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$@"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@, %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@, %@ quality" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of a voice in the voice pop-up. %1$@ is the voice's name and %2$@ is its quality, such as Enhanced.\nWhat VoiceOver says for a voice in the voice sheet's menu. %1$@ is the voice's name; %2$@ is its quality, such as Enhanced.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@, %2$@ quality"
