    "In Library" : {
      "comment" : "The note on a feed's episode or article row that was moved into the library as a book of its own. Title case.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "En la biblioteca"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In Library windows, a letter alone moves to the first book or folder starting with it, so a shortcut that is a letter alone, such as W, works only in other windows." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Shortcuts tab of Settings. In a Library window, a letter key pressed with no other key jumps to the first book or folder starting with that letter, so a shortcut made of a letter alone, such as W, cannot work in a Library window.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "En las ventanas de la biblioteca, una letra sola va al primer libro o carpeta que empieza con ella, así que un atajo que es una sola letra, como W, funciona únicamente en otras ventanas."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Nelle finestre della libreria, una lettera da sola porta al primo libro o alla prima cartella che inizia con essa, quindi una scorciatoia fatta di una sola lettera, come W, funziona solo nelle altre finestre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In Progress" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A reading state as the pop-up names it. This is the case .inProgress.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "En curso"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "In corso"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a regular expression, a dollar sign and a group's number, as in $1 or $2, put back what that group matched." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the replacement field in the substitution rule editor. $1 and $2 are written as in regular expressions and stay as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "En una expresión regular, un signo de dólar seguido del número de un grupo, como $1 o $2, repone lo que ese grupo encontró."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "In un’espressione regolare, il simbolo del dollaro seguito dal numero di un gruppo, come $1 o $2, reinserisce il testo trovato da quel gruppo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In at %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said as the audio editor's Mark In marks the selection's start. %@ is the time in words. A sentence about the selection it makes may follow.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
