          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth si è chiuso per proteggere il tuo Mac"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth Subscriptions" : {
      "comment" : "The title written into an exported OPML file of subscriptions. Title case.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Suscripciones de TextMouth"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth attaches WebVTT (.vtt) and SubRip (.srt) files." : {
      "comment" : "Alert explaining why a chosen file was not attached as a transcript. WebVTT and SubRip are subtitle file formats, and .vtt and .srt their file extensions.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth hängt WebVTT-Dateien (.vtt) und SubRip-Dateien (.srt) an."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth adjunta archivos WebVTT (.vtt) y SubRip (.srt)."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth allega file WebVTT (.vtt) e SubRip (.srt)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert %@ files because its converter is missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: the converter TextMouth carries is missing from the app, which only a damaged copy is. %@ is the name of the file's format, such as WMA or Matroska. Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede convertir archivos %@ porque falta su conversor en la app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert the sound of “%@”: it is in a kind of audio it does not read." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its sound is in a codec TextMouth does not decode. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede convertir el sonido de “%@”: está en un tipo de audio que no lee."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert “%@”: its sound changes rate or channels partway through, by more than it can follow." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its sound changes its sample rate or its number of channels partway through, by more than the converter can follow. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede convertir “%@”: su sonido cambia de frecuencia o de canales a mitad del archivo, más de lo que puede seguir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert “%@”: part of its sound is in one piece too large to decode." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: one frame of its sound holds more samples than TextMouth decodes at once. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede convertir “%@”: una parte de su sonido está en un fragmento demasiado grande para decodificarse."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't play this kind of file (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed's episode could not be downloaded: the file is of a kind TextMouth does not play. %@ is the file's type or extension, such as audio/x-flac.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede reproducir este tipo de archivo (%@)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't read the audio file %@ because %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: it is of a format TextMouth reads, in a form it refuses. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the reason, a clause in English that follows \"because\" and has no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't read the audio file %1$@ because %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer el archivo de audio %1$@ porque %2$@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth non può leggere il file audio %@ perché %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't read the folder %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why the chosen folder can't be used: it can't be read. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$@ is the reason in a few words, such as \"permission denied\", with no full stop.\nWhy the library can't be used: its folder can't be read. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$@ is the reason in a few words, such as \"permission denied\", with no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't read the folder %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer la carpeta %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth non riesce a leggere la cartella %@: %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't read this kind of picture (%@). Save it as a PNG or JPEG, then import that copy." : {
      "comment" : "Why a picture was refused at import: a kind of picture the system knows but TextMouth does not decode. %@ is the system's description of the kind, such as \"DNG image\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer este tipo de imagen (%@). Guárdala como PNG o JPEG y luego importa esa copia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't read “%@” as %@. It may be damaged, or named for another format." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its bytes are not of the format its name says, or are damaged. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the name of the format its name says, such as WMA or AVI video.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't read “%1$@” as %2$@. It may be damaged, or named for another format."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer “%1$@” como %2$@. Puede estar dañado o tener el nombre de otro formato."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't safely read the file “%@” in this book, because it defines entities of its own." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a file inside an EPUB or DAISY book was refused: it defines XML entities of its own, which could make it far larger when read. %@ is the file's path inside the book.",
      "localizations" : {
