                  "value" : "TextMouth è aperto anche su “%@” (attivo %lld minuti fa)."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is also open on “%@” (active less than a minute ago)." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the warning that another Mac has this library open. %@ is that Mac's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth también está abierto en «%@» (activo hace menos de un minuto)."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth è aperto anche su “%@” (attivo meno di un minuto fa)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is finishing up before it quits: %@. It quits when that is done." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text and announcement while TextMouth finishes work before quitting. %@ is the list of what is under way, such as \"saving the library and keeping downloads\", already joined in the language's own list style.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está terminando antes de salir: %@. Saldrá cuando termine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta ultimando le operazioni prima di uscire: %@. Uscirà al termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is getting them now, and the library opens when they arrive." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why the library can't be used yet: the files are being fetched from the cloud, and the library opens by itself when they arrive. \"Them\" means the library's files named in the sentence before.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los está obteniendo ahora, y la biblioteca se abre cuando lleguen."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth li sta ottenendo ora e la libreria si aprirà quando arriveranno."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: books are being moved between folders.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está moviendo libros entre carpetas."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta spostando libri tra le cartelle."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is moving books between folders. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está moviendo libros entre carpetas. Espera a que termine y vuelve a elegir %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta spostando libri tra le cartelle. Attendi che finisca, poi scegli di nuovo %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is not downloading right now." : {
      "comment" : "Why the download of a feed's next episode did not start: the app is quitting or the feed is being deleted. Said after \"The next episode could not be downloaded, so playback stopped.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no está descargando en este momento."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth non sta scaricando in questo momento."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay unsaved in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save stays unsaved: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the changes that could not be saved.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está abriendo de nuevo con otra biblioteca, así que siguen sin guardarse en esta."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth si sta riaprendo su un’altra libreria, quindi restano non salvate in questa."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay where they are in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files stays undone: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está abriendo de nuevo con otra biblioteca, así que siguen donde están en esta."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth si sta riaprendo su un’altra libreria, quindi restano dove sono in questa."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is quitting and the book's audio doesn't hold these edits yet. Discard undoes them; next time you edit this book, Redo brings them back until you make another edit. Cancel keeps TextMouth open." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the question about the audio editor's unsaved edits asked as TextMouth quits: what Discard and Cancel do.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth wird beendet, und das Audio des Buchs enthält diese Bearbeitungen noch nicht. „Verwerfen“ widerruft sie; wenn du dieses Buch das nächste Mal bearbeitest, bringt „Wiederholen“ sie zurück, bis du erneut bearbeitest. „Abbrechen“ lässt TextMouth geöffnet."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está cerrando y el audio del libro aún no contiene estas ediciones. Descartar las deshace; la próxima vez que edites este libro, Rehacer las recupera hasta que hagas otra edición. Cancelar mantiene TextMouth abierto."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta per chiudersi e l’audio del libro non contiene ancora queste modifiche. Scarta le annulla; la prossima volta che modifichi questo libro, Ripeti le riporta indietro finché non fai un’altra modifica. Annulla mantiene TextMouth aperto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading the library's text again. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why a book can't be read again while the library's text is being read again (the launch batch, Redo Text Extraction), in the words TextMouth uses while its storage work is held (StorageBusyError).",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer el texto de la biblioteca. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta rileggendo il testo della libreria. Riprova quando ha finito."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again in another encoding. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again in another encoding, in the same words as extractionRefusal: a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otra codificación. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta rileggendo «%@» con un’altra codifica. Riprova quando ha finito."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with another braille code. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with another braille code, as the other re-reads' sentences say it (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:), BrailleFileCodeWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otro código braille. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta rileggendo «%@» con un altro codice braille. Riprova quando ha finito."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with other braille file characters. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with other braille file characters, as the encoding's sentence says it for any other book (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)): a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otros caracteres de archivo braille. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta rileggendo «%@» con altri caratteri del file braille. Riprova quando ha finito."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: the library is being rebuilt.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reconstruyendo su directorio de datos."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta ricostruendo la sua cartella dei dati."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory, the folder that holds the library. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reconstruyendo su directorio de datos. Espera a que termine y vuelve a elegir %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta ricostruendo la sua cartella dei dati. Attendi che finisca, poi scegli di nuovo %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is replacing “%@” with the new copy. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Why an action on a book is refused while Replace Existing makes the new copy ready, such as Edit Text or opening the book. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reemplazando “%@” por la copia nueva. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still carrying out your last answer. Wait until it finishes." : {
      "comment" : "What an import question says when it is answered again while the previous answer is still being carried out.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sigue procesando tu última respuesta. Espera a que termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still saving them." : {
      "comment" : "The reason that ends \"Changes to the feed “Planet Money” could not be saved:\" in the quit prompt and banner. Them are the feed's changes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth todavía los está guardando."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sigue usando %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta ancora usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is switching to another library and opening again on it." : {
      "comment" : "Why an operation was refused: TextMouth is switching to another library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está cambiando a otra biblioteca y se abrirá de nuevo con ella."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sta passando a un’altra libreria e si sta riaprendo su di essa."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to make changes in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen location can't be used: macOS does not let TextMouth write there. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para hacer cambios en %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth non è autorizzato a fare modifiche in %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to post notifications. Turn them on in System Settings, Notifications, TextMouth." : {
      "comment" : "What the notifications setting's help says while macOS does not allow TextMouth to post notifications. System Settings and Notifications are macOS's own names, in the language of macOS.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para enviar notificaciones. Actívalas en Ajustes del Sistema, Notificaciones, TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to use the microphone. Turn it on in System Settings, Privacy & Security, Microphone." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when macOS has denied TextMouth the microphone. Names the places in System Settings, as macOS words them, where the user can allow it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth darf das Mikrofon nicht verwenden. Aktiviere es in den Systemeinstellungen unter „Datenschutz & Sicherheit“, „Mikrofon“."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para usar el micrófono. Actívalo en Ajustes del Sistema, Privacidad y seguridad, Micrófono."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth non può usare il microfono. Attivalo in Impostazioni di Sistema, Privacy e sicurezza, Microfono."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth keeps the original file of audio it converts at import. An original takes about as much disk space as its converted file, or twice as much when uncompressed. Export offers it as the Original file. A feed episode's original is not kept: it can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Keep Originals switch while it is on. \"Original file\" names the choice Export offers; keep it the same as that choice's translation.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth conserva el archivo original del audio que convierte al importar. Un original ocupa casi tanto espacio en disco como su archivo convertido, o el doble si no está comprimido. Exportar lo ofrece como Archivo original. El original de un episodio de un canal no se conserva: se puede descargar de nuevo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth kept the text you changed in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the message when an automatic rebuild left a book's edited text alone. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth conservó el texto que cambiaste en %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth ha conservato il testo modificato in %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left it there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when one item appeared: TextMouth left the item and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.\nSecond sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth left what was put there and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth lo dejó allí y sigue usando %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth l’ha lasciato lì e sta ancora usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which hold no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that hold no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.spx” and “b.spx”\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que no contienen sonido que pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which holds no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that holds no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que no contiene sonido que pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which need TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.avi” and “b.wmv”\". Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que necesitan el conversor de TextMouth, que falta en la app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which needs TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes. Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que necesita el conversor de TextMouth, que falta en la app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left them there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when several items appeared: TextMouth left the items and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los dejó allí y sigue usando %@."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth li ha lasciati lì e sta ancora usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth makes a folder named after the feed in %@, and its episodes and articles download into it." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the folder picker of the Add Feed sheet. %@ is the library folder chosen, or the name of the library's top level.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth crea en %@ una carpeta con el nombre del canal, y sus episodios y artículos se descargan en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth makes a new library index from the books in this folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before opening the library without its index file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth crea un índice nuevo de la biblioteca con los libros de esta carpeta."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth crea un nuovo indice della libreria dai libri in questa cartella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with a problem:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about one book that moved into the current library format with a problem. %@ is a count of books, such as \"1 book\". The book's line follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth pasó %@ al formato actual de la biblioteca, pero con un problema:"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth ha spostato %@ nel formato di libreria attuale, ma con un problema:"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with problems:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about several books that moved into the current library format with problems. %@ is a count of books, such as \"3 books\". The books' lines follow.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth pasó %@ al formato actual de la biblioteca, pero con problemas:"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth ha spostato %@ nel formato di libreria attuale, ma con dei problemi:"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of four or more duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %lld is the number of books. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copy of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld de copias nuevas de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld copia nueva de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld copias nuevas de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copies of %@ to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of two or three duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %@ is their titles in curly quotes, listed as a sentence lists them. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth movió a la Papelera las copias nuevas de %@, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copy of “%@” to the Trash, because the question whether to keep it as a duplicate was never answered before TextMouth closed. To get it back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copy of one duplicate book to the Trash, because its question was never answered. %@ is the book's title. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth movió a la Papelera la copia nueva de “%@”, porque no se respondió la pregunta sobre si conservarlo como duplicado antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlo, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once it has finished moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when books have been moved between folders. \"Them\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los devuelve cuando termine de mover libros entre carpetas."
