    },
    "The Mac's speech engine refused to speak part of “%@”, even with its brackets made silent." : {
      "comment" : "Why a chapter of a spoken audio export could not be spoken. %@ is the chapter's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El motor de voz de la Mac se negó a leer una parte de «%@», incluso con sus corchetes en silencio."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Il motore vocale del Mac ha rifiutato di leggere una parte di “%@”, anche con le parentesi silenziate."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The PDF file could not be opened." : {
      "comment" : "Why a PDF could not be imported: PDFKit could not open it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo abrir el archivo PDF."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Non è stato possibile aprire il file PDF."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The View pop-up of a Library window offers these views in this order. A new window opens at the first one offered." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the list is, and where a new window opens.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El menú Vista de una ventana de la biblioteca ofrece estas vistas en este orden. Una ventana nueva se abre en la primera que se ofrece."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Il menu Vista di una finestra della libreria propone queste viste in quest’ordine. Una nuova finestra si apre sulla prima proposta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The address of %@ doesn't hold a feed TextMouth can read." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed could not be refreshed or subscribed to: its address holds something that is not a feed, such as a web page. %@ is the feed's title or server.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La dirección de %@ no contiene un canal que TextMouth pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive also holds %lld other books that were not imported; unzip it to import them." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the notice about an archive that holds other books than the one imported. %lld is the number of other books.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The archive also holds %lld other book that was not imported; unzip it to import it."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The archive also holds %lld other books that were not imported; unzip it to import them."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo comprimido también contiene %lld de libros más que no se importaron; descomprímelo para importarlos."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo comprimido también contiene %lld libro más que no se importó; descomprímelo para importarlo."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo comprimido también contiene %lld libros más que no se importaron; descomprímelo para importarlos."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive expands to %@, but the disk holding the TextMouth library has only %@ free, and TextMouth keeps %@ of it free." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an import's archive was refused for want of disk space. %1$@ is the size the archive expands to; %2$@ is the free space; %3$@ is the space TextMouth keeps free.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The archive expands to %1$@, but the disk holding the TextMouth library has only %2$@ free, and TextMouth keeps %3$@ of it free."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido se expande a %1$@, pero el disco que contiene la biblioteca de TextMouth solo tiene %2$@ libres, y TextMouth mantiene %3$@ libres."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio si espande a %@, ma il disco che contiene la libreria di TextMouth ha solo %@ liberi, e TextMouth ne mantiene liberi %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive expands to %@, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts from archives holding audio or other archives." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused. %1$@ is the size the archive expands to, such as \"2 GB\"; %2$@ is the limit for archives that hold audio or other archives.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The archive expands to %1$@, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts from archives holding audio or other archives."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido se expande a %1$@, más de los %2$@ que TextMouth extrae de archivos comprimidos con audio u otros archivos comprimidos."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio si espande a %@, più dei %@ che TextMouth estrae da archivi contenenti audio o altri archivi."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive expands to %@, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts from archives without audio." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused. %1$@ is the size the archive expands to, such as \"2 GB\"; %2$@ is the limit for archives that hold no audio.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The archive expands to %1$@, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts from archives without audio."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido se expande a %1$@, más de los %2$@ que TextMouth extrae de archivos comprimidos sin audio."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio si espande a %@, più dei %@ che TextMouth estrae da archivi senza audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive holds %@ files and folders, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts in one import." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused: it holds too many files and folders. %1$@ is how many it holds, already formatted; %2$@ is the limit, already formatted.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The archive holds %1$@ files and folders, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts in one import."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido contiene %1$@ archivos y carpetas, más de los %2$@ que TextMouth extrae en una importación."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio contiene %@ file e cartelle, più dei %@ che TextMouth estrae in una sola importazione."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive holds a file whose path leads outside it, which is never extracted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an archive was refused at import: it holds a file whose path climbs out of the folder it is extracted into.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido contiene un archivo cuya ruta sale de él, que nunca se extrae."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive holds a link to a file outside it, which is never extracted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an archive was refused at import: it holds a symbolic link to a file outside it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido contiene un enlace a un archivo fuera de él, que nunca se extrae."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive holds more than the %@ it declares, so extraction stopped." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an import's archive stopped extracting: it holds more than it declares. %@ is the size it declares, such as \"2 GB\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido contiene más de los %@ que declara, así que la extracción se detuvo."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio contiene più dei %@ dichiarati, quindi l’estrazione si è interrotta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive is damaged, incomplete, or not a ZIP archive." : {
      "comment" : "Why an archive was refused at import: it could not be read as a ZIP archive.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido está dañado, incompleto o no es un archivo ZIP."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The archive “%@” inside it expands to %@, but the disk holding the TextMouth library has only %@ free, and TextMouth keeps %@ of it free." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an import's archive was refused for want of disk space, when the archive is inside another. %1$@ is the inner archive's name; %2$@ is the size it expands to; %3$@ is the free space; %4$@ is the space TextMouth keeps free.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The archive “%1$@” inside it expands to %2$@, but the disk holding the TextMouth library has only %3$@ free, and TextMouth keeps %4$@ of it free."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo comprimido «%1$@» de su interior se expande a %2$@, pero el disco que contiene la biblioteca de TextMouth solo tiene %3$@ libres, y TextMouth mantiene %4$@ libres."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’archivio “%@” al suo interno si espande a %@, ma il disco che contiene la libreria di TextMouth ha solo %@ liberi, e TextMouth ne mantiene liberi %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The article leaves the list for good, and its download, if any, is deleted." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the confirmation before an article is deleted from its feed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El artículo sale de la lista para siempre, y su descarga, si la tiene, se elimina."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The article leaves the list for good; the book it became in your library stays." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the confirmation before an article that was moved into the library is deleted from its feed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El artículo sale de la lista para siempre; el libro en que se convirtió en tu biblioteca se queda."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio can't be edited" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert saying the audio editor couldn't open.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Das Audio kann nicht bearbeitet werden"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se puede editar el audio"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Impossibile modificare l’audio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio converted from %@ could not be given its name." : {
      "comment" : "Why a converted audio file was refused: it could not be given its final name. %@ is the source file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo poner nombre al audio convertido de %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio converted from %@ could not be written (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Why converted audio was not saved as an .m4a file. %1$@ is the source file's name and %2$@ the error's domain and code, in the system's words.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The audio converted from %1$@ could not be written (%2$@)."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo escribir el audio convertido de %1$@ (%2$@)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio converted from %@ failed its check: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a converted audio file was refused: it failed the check made after conversion. %1$@ is the source file's name and %2$@ the reason, a phrase with no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The audio converted from %1$@ failed its check: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio convertido de %1$@ no superó su comprobación: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio couldn't be exported." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor's export fails. A sentence giving the reason follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Das Audio konnte nicht exportiert werden."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo exportar el audio."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Impossibile esportare l’audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio file that the edits need can't be read as audio.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Das Audio konnte nicht gelesen werden."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer el audio."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Impossibile leggere l’audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio editor" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Works in pop-up of a keyboard shortcut: the shortcut works only in the audio editor's windows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El editor de audio"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Editor audio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio editor for %@ is already open." : {
      "comment" : "Said when Edit Audio… is chosen for a book whose editor is already open; that window comes forward. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Der Audioeditor für %@ ist bereits geöffnet."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El editor de audio de %@ ya está abierto."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "L’editor audio di %@ è già aperto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ could not be read for converting." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: it could not be read as audio, or it is only in the cloud. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer el archivo de audio %@ para convertirlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ ends before its audio does, so it could not be converted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: the file stops before the audio its header promises. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ termina antes que su audio, así que no se pudo convertir."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Il file audio %@ termina prima del suo audio, quindi non è stato possibile convertirlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ has %lld channels but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file was not converted: it has more than two channels and does not say which is which, so a mix to stereo would keep two arbitrary channels. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$lld the number of channels, always more than two.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The audio file %@ has %lld channel but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The audio file %@ has %lld channels but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld de canales pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld canal pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld canales pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ is damaged, so it could not be converted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: a checksum failed or a field holds a value no encoder writes. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ está dañado, así que no se pudo convertir."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Il file audio %@ è danneggiato, quindi non è stato possibile convertirlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ is not the kind of file its name says." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: its bytes are not of the format its extension names. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ no es del tipo que indica su nombre."
